From eceda69ddfd1bb15d27bd803c3945fefb6fd402d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DanielBeeck <daniel.beck99@outlook.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:29:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] hidpp20: support the Logitech G502 X LIGHTSPEED

The G502 X LIGHTSPEED (usb:046d:409f through the LIGHTSPEED receiver,
usb:046d:c098 wired) was rejected by the hidpp20 driver for three reasons:

- it reports onboard profile format 0x0a. The sector layout verified on
  the device matches the known G402/G502X layout (255 byte sectors with
  the CRC in the last two bytes), so accept that format id.
- it only implements 0x2202 (Extended Adjustable DPI) instead of 0x2201.
  Add support for the feature: the sensor count, capabilities, the DPI
  range stream (plain values and 0xe000 | step markers across several
  replies) and the current DPI parameters. Ranges are kept per sensor
  and validated with hidpp20_sensor_accepts_dpi().
- it only implements 0x8061 (Extended Adjustable Report Rate) instead
  of 0x8060, which left the report rate list empty and made libratbag
  drop the device. Add the feature; rates are indices for 125 << n Hz.
  Onboard profiles store milliseconds, so only rates up to 1000Hz are
  offered on profile based devices.

Also allocate at least 256 bytes for a profile sector so the 256 byte
hidpp20_internal_profile union never overruns a 255 byte buffer, and
expose the ROM profiles as enabled when a device has no valid profile
directory yet, which is what the firmware runs on in that state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
